// DISCRIMINATOR ROWS DELETED 2026-08-11 (gunbc#8146, review 51152). Four rows
// named discriminating tests — verified_lookup_refuses_artifact_replaced_after_probe,
// v3_write_refuses_when_verified_artifact_already_present,
// legacy_v1_cold_rebuild_migrates_to_v3_on_fresh_index,
// cross_process_cache_matches_cold_oracle_corpus — all of which lived in
// resolve_cross_process_cache_test.rs, deleted by this PR. Their witness only
// substring-matched the constants against themselves, so it proved the strings
// were spelled a certain way and nothing about any test existing or running: a
// false executing receipt (DESIGN §5).
//
// The witness-side row that read those four constants,
// resolved_graph_cache_hand_rust_discriminating_tests_named, was deleted in the same
// change and for the same reason. Its record lived as trailing prose in
// dag/test/claim/resolved_graph_cache_hand_rust_witness_test.dag, attached to no module
// item — the one shape DESIGN §4c cannot admit — so it is consolidated here, where the
// deletion it describes is already recorded.
//
// They are DELETED rather than re-pointed because there is nothing to point at
// — a corpus search finds those names only in these strings. Naming a test that
// does not exist is worse than naming none. The discriminating evidence for this
// scaffold is now exactly the census below, which joins each path to a readable
// file, plus the retained materialization_provider_resolved_graph_consumer_test.
